{
 "about": "What Chrome for Testing 155.0.8059.79 ImageDecoder gives for the files in png-webp/ (and test.png, wpt/four-colors.*): frames as \"<format> <width>x<height> <timestamp> <duration> <first 16 hex digits of the SHA-256 of the copyTo() bytes>\" (\"ok <format>\" where only the format was kept), errors as \"<name>: <message>\" (only the name where our message is worded differently). whole: BufferSource, decode() of every frame and one past the end. sweeps: a stream left open with the first N bytes, for every N: [first N, tracks.ready, the track [animated, frameCount, repetitionCount]] each time either changes. edges: a stream left open: the first N where decode({frameIndex}) settles, and with what (null: never). ends: the first N bytes, then the end of the stream: tracks.ready, completed, the track, then [frameIndex, result] of each decode() in order. afterReady: a decode() made right after tracks.ready resolves, then a decode() of each next frame once the last settled: buffer from a BufferSource (and one past the end), stream from one chunk with every byte on a stream left open (no decode() past the last frame there: Chrome waits for more data).",
